x86_64-linux  cxx1's listing carries three names clang's does not: _ZN2B2D1Ev, _ZN2C2D1Ev and _ZN2D2D1Ev - the implicit destructors this case exists to make exist. cxx1 emits an implicit member as an ordinary definition; clang emits it linkonce_odr in a comdat, which the collector does not see. The same difference dynamic-cast.nonames and range-for-class.nonames record, and older than this case. What is *not* a difference is whether they exist: before this round B2's was emitted by nobody and the program failed to link.
arm64-darwin  the same difference and one name of it, __ZN2B2D1Ev. Only the intermediate class's shows here, C2's and D2's being named by clang's listing too - measured, and not reasoned from the Linux line above, which lists three.
